Z||000004||DavidHenshaw||10-24-2000||05:23 PM||||Lets face it Ken. Most of the students in your class don't know much about cars, especially the coeds. Consequently their opinion of an automobile is based mostly on what a particular car looks like. Of course, there are some nice looking cars out there but how many of them can compare to the Fiero GT or the SE for that matter. <P>Whether we Fiero owners are aware of it or not we are driving a thing of timeless beauty. Just take some photos of your car and pass them around. If some of the class can't see the inherent wisdom of your choice in autos, well they will just have to live like that until they see the light.<P>Pardon me for being long here. We all know there are some other beautiful cars, most of them manufactured in Italy and costing so much only the wealthy can afford. There are also lots of cars pretending to be beautiful. IMHO about 2/3 of Corvette production through the years falls into that catagory. Forgive if I've offended any who own Vetts. <P>Fiero forever!!! <P><BR>Dave<P>86 GT fastback||||reg||1
Z||000005||gixxer||10-24-2000||06:14 PM||||Easy.<BR>-Point out the general and specific technical design DIFFERENCES between the Fiero and the typical U.S. passenger car of the mid '80s.<BR>-State how these differences in layout and design will favor the Fiero in regards to all types of performance (fuel mileage, acceleration, handling, safety, etc).<BR>-Show how these performance gains will contribute to a enhanced sense of well being, safety, better hair days, world peace...   <BR> ||||reg||1
