Z||000007||Fformula88||10-24-2000||08:19 PM||||Gixxer has a good point with the "technical" differences.  The build process was a revolutionary achievement by Pontiac.  The use of the "Mill and Drill" process to attach the plastic bodies (ennduraflex body panels was another achievement) ensured exact body fit.  It heavily influenced future GM cars.  The 1990-1996 GM minivan trio (Trans Sport, Lumina, Sillouhette) was also built using the enduraflex panels.  All Saturns use these panels except for the hood/roof/trunk and the GM F-Bodies even use them for front fenders and doors.  <P>The Fiero is also the only American mid-engine sports car.  So it is unique to the American auto industry.  <P>Good luck on your paper!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
